id: pm-context-task-phase-contracts
title: Keep mandatory task-phase context fields and explain phase switches
description: "Explicit investigation, implementation, review and handoff requirements over authoritative SDK field reads, with lossless compact packets and unchanged SDK session references."
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-26T02:25:01.719Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T22:12:24.194Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Four phase fixtures preserve every mandatory field or refuse; unrelated fields are omitted with restore selectors; one phase switch reuses unchanged SDK session references.
comments[30]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T02:25:10.836Z",codex-agent,"Plan: one strict bounded request schema, typed SDK and context-phase command, all-or-refuse mandatory fields, exact omission restoration, SDK sessions keyed by item/field/value so changed projections cannot reuse stale facts. Stateless caller-carried session input; no new tracker mutation, import/sync writer, journal, lease or shared checkpoint. Validate four phases, seeded 500-sequence SDK-read model, extreme input/output values, installed no-git CLI, behavioral revert proof and read-only committed public snapshot. Local targeted tests/typecheck/docstrings; npm and Bun full gates in CI at unchanged thresholds. CLI registry reports 2026.10.25; retain package SDK pin 2026.10.23 per queue rules."
  "2026-10-26T02:36:27.982Z",codex,"Implementation uses SDK intent composition/resolution, SDK omission receipts and SDK session suppression/accounting over the existing cache-free freshness reader. Field facts bind target item, field and current SDK JSON value; new phase fields cannot alias older projections. Full metadata fixtures exposed SDK optional properties with undefined values in linked files/docs; accept only ordinary JSON omission of optional object properties, retain exact whitespace and relationships, reject sparse arrays/nonfinite values. Reference model reads SDK get output through standard JSON transport, with no handwritten normalization. Installed CLI testing also caught camelCase option normalization; all command overrides now accept the host-normalized keys."
  "2026-10-26T02:42:21.466Z",codex-agent,"Public committed snapshot 41fa36e1eae25b7ce692de6b9d198c0b05730acd: 93 items, 1794 source fields, 744 phase/format attempts; 658 successful packets, 84 MISSING_FIELD review refusals, 2 BUDGET_TOO_SMALL implementation refusals; 1316 exact mandatory-value checks, 11518 omission selectors, 92 successful switches reusing 92 unchanged SDK title references. JSON: 329 packets, 1168385 bytes, range 2245-7687; TOON: 329 packets, 983116 bytes, range 1885-6929. Read-only non-Git copy, no Git on PATH, all source hashes unchanged. Local strict tracker health reports existing installed pm-github host skew (pinned host 2026.10.23 versus extension 2026.10.25); verify fresh CI before attributing a gate failure to this feature. Prior progress comment inherited the project default author; subsequent writes explicitly use codex-agent."
  "2026-10-26T02:48:16.592Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: temporarily retain only the first mandatory field in buildPhaseContext; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"four real SDK phase fixtures\" test/task-phase.test.ts fails 1/1 (binding count 1 versus 2). Restore, then temporarily bypass only SDK reference suppression; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"phase switches reuse unchanged\" test/task-phase.test.ts fails 1/1 on the shared title reference. Exact source bytes restored after both probes. Initial full seeded model passed 500 sequences and 2500 packet operations; optimizing the reference reads to explicit SDK fields avoids repeatedly computing unrelated child/history facets. New concurrency fixtures use one non-Git tracker and preserve a foreign runtime record across independent readers for all four status-role families."
  "2026-10-26T02:51:09.627Z",codex-agent,"Local final targeted validation: task-phase suite 8/8, renderer ownership 7/7, no skips. Targeted c8 task-phase.ts coverage is 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. Seeded model: 500 sequences, 2500 packet operations with explicit SDK field read-back; includes old requests, old sessions, CRLF, native collections and relationships. Concurrent readers test 8 independent sessions for each of four custom status-role families on one plain tracker; all foreign/source bytes unchanged. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run docstring and git diff --check pass. No lint script is defined; docstring gate is the package source-style gate. pm test --run --progress --only-last passed the linked four-phase fixture 1/1; test-result tracking is disabled, so this comment retains the execution receipt without changing tracking policy. Full npm/Bun release gates are delegated to CI per the host-load instruction. Rechecked installed CLI 2026.10.25 SDK declarations: intents/sessions still provide projection/reuse without phase-mandatory field retention."
  "2026-10-26T02:57:36.398Z",codex-agent,"First CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/40261234444 passed fresh tracker health, build-current checks and all eight phase tests at 100% module coverage. The full suite found one older exact command-registration assertion missing context-phase (418/419 tests passed), and native coverage exposed CLI override branches previously exercised only in installed subprocesses. Updated that registration assertion and added both kebab-case and host-normalized camelCase option overrides through the real extension harness, including explicit format precedence over global JSON. No feature behavior, thresholds or dependencies changed. The old receipt-error fallback remains an existing c8 branch gap; recheck the full unchanged gate after these new-path fixes."
  "2026-10-26T03:02:23.947Z",codex-agent,"Second CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/40261687756 passed all 419 tests on both Node versions, with phase module still at 100% coverage. The native 100% branch gate identified one remaining phase CLI refusal branch covered only by the subprocess test: a JSON root that is null, an array or a scalar. Added those three malformed request cases through both source and compiled extension harnesses. The first two CI runs are failure evidence, not release-gate passes. No thresholds or product behavior changed; rerun npm and Bun full gates at the corrected head."
  "2026-10-26T03:08:12.653Z",codex-agent,"Both npm release gates pass on Node 22 and 26 at f3ea0a3 in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/40262200866; Bun gates are still running. Boundary review found a related strict-input gap: the shared legacy option helper trimmed blank CLI overrides into absence, silently retaining a packet phase or default budget. The phase CLI adapter now preserves raw override values and lets its one strict request schema refuse blanks/nulls/wrong types. Added five real installed blank-flag cases and source/compiled harness refusals; positive installed packets also preserve a mandatory body over 6 KB. Focused CLI and registration checks pass 2/2. Final npm/Bun gate evidence must use the subsequent corrected head."
  "2026-10-26T03:08:58.223Z",codex-agent,"Strict CLI override revert proof: replace only the raw phase/format adapter read with the previous trim-and-ignore helper; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"installed CLI\" test/task-phase.test.ts fails 1/1 with Missing expected rejection for a blank phase in the source extension host. Exact source bytes restored afterward. The positive final adapter had already passed the installed CLI and registration checks 2/2, including the larger mandatory body and both alias spellings. All five blank CLI flags now reach the single request schema and refuse instead of being ignored."
  "2026-10-26T03:15:54.977Z",codex-agent,"Verified full CI success at product head 3508a58851cba2709055a1d169f4fbeaac26f715: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/40262690108 . npm run release:check and bun run release:check both pass on Node 22 and 26: 419/419 tests per gate, zero failures or skips (1676 aggregate passes). Native coverage covers 15 sources at 100% lines/branches/functions. c8: 100% statements/functions/lines, 99.95% branches, unchanged 99.9% branch threshold; task-phase.ts remains 100% in all four dimensions. Fresh tracker health, build-current, dependency audit, package dry run, changelog, publication-attestation and CodeQL checks pass. Current-build public validation reran with identical 93-item/744-attempt numbers and unchanged source hashes. Ready PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/pull/181 . Automated review approval is unavailable: CodeRabbit auto-review disabled, Sourcery quota exhausted, Greptile trial ended; their statuses do not supply review approval. Item remains in_progress and released for orchestrator verification; do not merge or release the package."
  "2026-10-26T14:13:35.964Z",codex-agent,"Blocking read-only review of PR 181 identified shell injection through an omitted metadata key in restore_with. Extend this item with class-wide command provenance: one structured argv builder and one POSIX argument quoting function; add argv fields alongside display strings in phase bindings/omission receipts, handoff/pack refreshes, file-focus guides and delta recovery commands. Refuse legacy free-form command overrides rather than evaluating or guessing shell syntax. Audit all runtime command suggestions, route static executable examples too, and distinguish explanatory prose from executable suggestions. Add seeded adversarial key/value shell round trips and the fixed semicolon case, prove no side effects, record a behavioral interpolation revert, run targeted checks and unchanged npm/Bun CI gates. Current npm CLI registry is 2026.10.26; retain the pinned SDK."
  "2026-10-26T14:25:51.699Z",codex-agent,"Class-wide implementation now starts with dense bounded argv and renders through one POSIX single-quote function. Phase bindings and omissions carry restore_argv; handoffs carry suggestedArgv; pack refresh/link examples carry command+argv objects; file-focus appends raw refresh argv; delta recovery carries command+argv and SDK suggested_retry_args. Legacy suggestedCommand shell-string input refuses with a structured-array remedy. Static registered help examples route through the same builder. Existing SDK quoteCommandArg uses a different double-quote policy, so it cannot satisfy the explicit POSIX single-quote contract. Core SDK session receipts expose an unquoted placeholder restore template and no argv; suppress that template from the package wire format, provide session_restore command+argv, and retain conservative SDK charging for the internal legacy template. New renderer coverage is 100/100/100/100; three command tests, including 500 seeded shell splits and real non-Git metadata, pass."
  "2026-10-26T14:30:08.396Z",codex-agent,"Interpolation revert proof: restore only the omitted-key restore_with interpolation in buildPhaseContext, keeping the new restore_argv and all tests. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"fixed review key\" test/suggested-command.test.ts fails 1/1: the real shell returns field a instead of a;printf X and loses the trailing budget arguments. Source restored exactly; the property suite passes 3/3 with the builder. Broader targeted checks pass except expected snapshots that required unnecessary quotes around plain Git tokens; updated them to the required minimal quoting. Public snapshot rerun still yields 93 items, 744 attempts, 658 successes, 86 typed refusals, 1316 retained mandatory values, 11518 omission selectors and 92 reused references, with unchanged source bytes. Added argv transport costs: JSON 1801950 bytes (3305-10741), TOON 1772334 bytes (3214-10651), 329 successes each."
  "2026-10-26T14:33:52.801Z",codex-agent,"Targeted validation for the review correction: command/pack/renderer suites pass 62/62; selected phase preservation/reuse/output/installed CLI tests pass 4/4; the real Git refresh regression passes 1/1 after updating minimally quoted plain-token expectations. Context receipt and delta production checks passed; no product regressions were hidden by snapshot updates. npm run build, npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run docstring and changelog checks pass. The package has no standalone lint script. pm test --run --progress --only-last executes the new command suite 3/3; tracking remains disabled, so this comment retains the receipt. Runtime-source grep found no remaining generated pm commands built with data interpolation or concatenation: only the shared builder/rendered output remains. Await final full npm/Bun CI before claiming complete gates."
  "2026-10-26T14:42:45.784Z",codex-agent,"The argv-first correction at df1884c passes all four full npm/Bun CI gates: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/40340975271 . Final wire inspection found one follow-up in the new typed file-focus refusal: its inherited legacy CommandError name prevents SDK expected-error recognition, risking loss of structured recovery metadata. Preserve the SDK canonical error name and assert isPmCliExpectedError; add an installed real unreadable-tracker JSON refusal test proving suggested_retry_args survives host serialization, then round-trip that DTO through TOON too. SDK default human-readable stderr is not a machine TOON document, so machine error consumers must request JSON or encode the SDK DTO. No upstream issue is filed. The new head must repeat full npm/Bun gates."
  "2026-10-26T14:45:29.282Z",codex-agent,"Final follow-up validation: the command suite still passes 3/3, including installed unreadable-tracker error JSON with executable recovery argv and DTO TOON round-trip. Preserve the SDK expected-error marker; the new assertion fails if the old CommandError name is restored. Also reject malformed Unicode as well as NUL, because POSIX UTF-8 argv cannot preserve those inputs exactly. The renderer remains 100/100/100/100 under targeted c8; typecheck, test typecheck, build and docstring checks pass. No standalone lint script exists. The public measurements remain the recorded argv-enabled figures because valid source data and phase projection behavior are unchanged. Release this claim and verify the pushed final head in npm/Bun CI."
  "2026-10-26T14:52:59.114Z",codex-agent,"Tightened the POSIX property oracle: require empty stderr and complete trailing NUL framing before comparing argv, so appended injected output cannot be discarded as an incomplete final record. All three command tests still pass. Restoring only omitted-key interpolation now fails the fixed review case 1/1 on the strict NUL-frame assertion (the injected printf suffix), and exact source bytes were restored. This strengthens the same quoting regression; no product behavior changes. The previous final-head CI is still queued and will be superseded by this test-only evidence commit; only the latest head can count as final gate evidence."
  "2026-10-26T19:13:01.051Z",codex-agent,"Re-review requires executable restoration selectors. Merged origin/main before further changes. Will derive supported projections from the pinned SDK, omit unsupported restore argv with a reason, execute receipt commands against a non-git tracker, and rerun focused plus full gates with at most two workers."
  "2026-10-26T19:25:02.249Z",codex-agent,"Execution validation passed all 115 emitted commands from four phases in both encodings against pinned pm 2026.10.23 outside Git; restored fields are checked against SDK-read values. Unsupported raw keys now emit UNSUPPORTED_FIELD_PROJECTION with no executable command. SDK get/list projection domains and configured runtime fields replace guessed selectors; aliases and derived facets do not restore raw metadata. JSON restoration preserves empty collections that the human TOON renderer omits. Concrete session refresh and help discovery replace runnable placeholder IDs. Public read-only corpus remains 93 items, 744 attempts, 658 successes, 86 refusals and 92 reused references, with source bytes unchanged."
  "2026-10-26T19:27:00.121Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: changed only restoreField to unconditionally return the previously guessed --fields command, keeping the tests and POSIX renderer. node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"fixed review key\" test/suggested-command.test.ts failed 1/1 because the exact emitted argv for a;printf X exited 2 with unknown_field_projection instead of 0. Restored the source bytes exactly in finally. The positive execution test also covers unknown ordinary fields, raw item aliases and derived-facet collisions so shell fidelity cannot substitute for restoration validity."
  "2026-10-26T19:37:31.697Z",codex-agent,"Latest command suite passed 4/4 through pm test --run --progress, including 115 exact phase commands and 28 installed package suggestions; zero failures or skips. The unreadable-registry regression passed 1/1. Initial three-file focused run passed 35/35, including the 500-sequence model. Public revalidation after the final selector derivation reproduces 1,904,622 JSON bytes and 1,875,006 TOON bytes over 329 packets each. Sequential full release gates enforce two test workers; npm is currently running. Typecheck, build, test typecheck, docstring and changelog checks passed; no separate lint script exists."
  "2026-10-26T19:41:08.658Z",codex-agent,"First full npm gate: all 427 tests passed with zero skips, but the unchanged native 100 percent branch gate rejected one uncovered settings-error branch (overall 99.96 percent; c8 99.92 percent). The SDK settings convenience read can return warning-bearing defaults, so malformed settings were refused later by the item reader. Reused the existing cache-free SDK-backed settings reader for projection discovery as well; it refuses warning-bearing or unstable sources before selectors are derived. The registry regression now requires the settings-specific remedy. Thresholds are unchanged; focused and full gates are being rerun."
  "2026-10-26T19:53:35.045Z",codex-agent,"Corrected npm run release:check passed at unchanged thresholds: 427/427 tests, zero failures or skips, native coverage 16 sources at 100 percent lines/branches/functions, c8 100 percent statements/functions/lines and 99.96 percent branches. The original SDK settings warning/default branch is covered through the shared authoritative reader. Audit, package dry run, workflow, docstring and publication/changelog guards passed. The Bun full gate is now running sequentially with the same two-worker cap."
  "2026-10-26T20:05:12.960Z",codex-agent,"Both corrected full release gates passed sequentially with at most two workers and fresh Git identities: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each 427/427, zero failures or skips. Native coverage reports 16 sources at 100 percent lines/branches/functions; c8 reports 100 percent statements/functions/lines and 99.96 percent branches at unchanged thresholds. Final public validation preserves all source bytes and reproduces the documented 93-item measurements. origin/main is merged and remains an ancestor. The pinned CLI execution test, 500-case shell property, 500-sequence SDK state model and behavioral revert proof are documented. Pushing the correction for exact-head CI; no merge or release."
  "2026-10-26T20:14:25.860Z",codex-agent,"Pushed product head 51f2be3d8d6612d09370a1e8f5aa27d8a8ce72a6 passes CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/40392580183: Node 22 and 26 each pass npm and Bun release:check at 427/427 tests, zero failures or skips (1708 aggregate). Both raw job logs confirm native coverage for 16 sources at 100 percent lines/branches/functions and c8 at 100 percent statements/functions/lines with 99.96 percent branches. Fresh tracker health, committed dist, audit, package, changelog and attestation checks pass; CodeQL run 40392580111 passes. A supplemental real pinned-CLI probe also accepts a generated refresh with a leading-dash tag. This evidence-only tracker/docs commit changes no product code; final head CI will be linked in PR 181. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item remains in_progress and unclosed."
  "2026-10-26T20:36:12.068Z",codex-agent,"Auto-round-1 finding is valid. General rule: a restoration selector must preserve the stored field meaning and value, not merely be accepted or exit zero. Audit of package source, SDK and CLI adapters, both codecs, refresh/help/recovery outputs and existing consumer tests finds one selector-discovery implementation shared by mandatory bindings and omissions. Runtime augmentation currently erases the native-metadata versus derived-selector distinction. Will derive the derived-only namespace from core SDK contracts before runtime registration, exclude it from restorations, and adversarially register every SDK-derived top-level name. Supplied review and available GitHub review/inline endpoints contain no other substantive or non-blocking finding; no finding is dismissed as false. origin/main is already merged and up to date; SDK remains pinned."
  "2026-10-26T20:52:34.994Z",codex-agent,"The class audit also found generic session recovery using get --depth brief; pinned get overwrites raw count metadata in that mode too. Session recovery now probes only canonical id, and bindings exclusively describe field recovery. New adversarial test derives all eight top-level collisions from SDK core contracts, registers every one, runs 500 deterministic state/replay models against literal values read back through the SDK, checks both encodings and all phases, and consumes the actual npm artifact under Node and Bun plus the installed CLI outside Git. Focused result: 1/1, six consumer packets, 78 emitted commands restore exact values. Revert proof 1: remove only the derived-namespace exclusion; test fails 1/1 on an invalid raw blockers restore. Revert proof 2: restore only the broad session recovery command; test fails 1/1 on its overwrite-capable projection. Source bytes restored exactly after each probe. Existing tests are retained unchanged."
  "2026-10-26T21:25:42.908Z",codex-agent,"Semantic-collision npm run release:check passed at unchanged thresholds: 428/428 tests, zero failures/skips; native coverage 16 sources at 100 percent lines/branches/functions; c8 100 percent statements/functions/lines and 99.96 percent branches. The additive registered-field property test passes inside the full gate; no prior test was edited or removed. Bun is running sequentially under the same two-worker cap. Public validation remains 93 items, 658/744 successes, 86 typed refusals, 1316 mandatory values and 92 reused references; source bytes unchanged."
  "2026-10-26T22:01:05.260Z",codex-agent,"Registered-collision correction complete. Both full local gates passed sequentially with two workers and fresh identities: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each 428/428, zero failures/skips. Native coverage 16 sources at 100 percent lines/branches/functions; c8 statements/functions/lines 100 percent, branches 99.96 percent at unchanged thresholds. Typecheck/build/test typecheck/docstring/changelog pass; no separate lint script exists. All eight registered derived-name collisions have no misleading command; session recovery is identity-only; mandatory source values remain intact. Additive adversarial test covers 500 SDK-read models, six real npm-artifact Node/Bun/CLI packets and 78 exact-value restorations outside Git. Both function-only reverts fail 1/1. Existing tests unchanged. Available review data contains no additional non-blocking findings. origin/main is still merged and current. Pushing for exact-head CI; no merge or release."
  "2026-10-26T22:12:22.023Z",codex-agent,"Registered-collision product head 9374a6e0d0b090b833e41c3749913943bb75d135 passes CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/40409245270: npm and Bun each pass 428/428 on Node 22 and 26, zero failures/skips (1712 aggregate). Raw logs confirm both native gates on both versions: 16 sources, 100 percent lines/branches/functions; c8 100 percent statements/functions/lines and 99.96 percent branches at unchanged thresholds. Fresh health, committed dist, audit, package, changelog and attestation checks pass; CodeQL run 40409244255 passes. The valid supplied blocker and the broad-session instance are fixed, with two independent failing revert proofs and no existing test changes. Available review sources contain no additional non-blocking finding. This final receipt commit changes only tracker/docs; exact final-head CI will be linked in PR 181. Item remains in_progress and unclosed for orchestrator verification."
